title: Operation Faustschlag
subtitle: The Germans are rapidly advancing!
new-page: true
max-visits: 1
tags: event
view-if: german_waiting_timer = 0 and german_negotiations = 3
on-arrival: enemy_front = best_enemy_front; front = best_front; attacking = 0; in_defensive_battle = 1; german_offensive_timer = 1 if refuse_treaty; instability += 10
set-jump: operation_faustschlag.post_battle
go-to: battle

= Operation Faustschlag

As it turns out, the Germans weren't bluffing at Brest-Litovsk. They have launched their offense, and their forces are rapidly advancing across the entire front, capturing an immense amount of territory. We are being informed that our own forces are crumbling at the sight of the enemy, with most retreating without putting up any resistance. Chaos and mass desertions are occurring all along the front. 

@post_battle
go-to: defeat_2 if battle_outcome = -2; defeat_1 if battle_outcome = -1; victory if battle_outcome >= 0
on-arrival: in_defensive_battle = 0; german_waiting_timer = 1;


@defeat_2
go-to: defeat_desc
on-arrival: {!
  Q.right_m_strength -= 5; Q.left_m_strength += 5; Q.m_strength += 5;
  Q.right_sr_strength -= 5; Q.sr_strength += 5; Q.lsr_strength += 10;
  Q.soldiers_lsr += 15; Q.soldiers_left_m += 5; Q.soldiers_sdi += 5;
  Q.soldiers_unrest += 15; Q.workers_unrest += 10; Q.peasants_unrest += 5;
  if (Q.german_negotiations >= 2) { Q.leftcom_strength -= 10; Q.leninist_strength += 5; }
  if (Q.b_in_gov == 1) { Q.soldiers_b -= 15; }
  if (Q.lsr_in_gov == 1) { Q.soldiers_lsr -= 5; }
  if (Q.sr_in_gov == 1) { Q.soldiers_sr -= 5; }            
  if (Q.m_in_gov == 1) { Q.soldiers_m -= 5; }
  if (Q.ns_in_gov == 1) { Q.soldiers_ns -= 5; }
  if (Q.sdi_in_gov == 1) { Q.soldiers_sdi -= 5; }
  Q.morale *= 0.8; Q.discipline *= 0.7; Q.train_capacity *= 0.85; Q.military_progress -= 2; Q.northern_progress -= 1; Q.western_progress = -3; Q.southwestern_progress = -3; 
!}

>Our casualties: [+ friendly_casualties +]0,000 troops

>Enemy casualties: [+ hostile_casualties +]0,000 troops


@defeat_1
go-to: defeat_desc
on-arrival: {!
  Q.right_m_strength -= 2.5; Q.left_m_strength += 2.5; Q.m_strength += 2.5;
  Q.right_sr_strength -= 2.5; Q.sr_strength += 2.5; Q.lsr_strength += 5;
  Q.soldiers_lsr += 7.5; Q.soldiers_left_m += 2.5; Q.soldiers_sdi += 2.5;
  Q.soldiers_unrest += 7.5; Q.workers_unrest += 5; Q.peasants_unrest += 2.5;
  if (german_negotiations >= 1) { Q.leftcom_strength -= 5; Q.leninist_strength += 2.5; }
  if (Q.b_in_gov == 1) { Q.soldiers_b -= 7.5; }
  if (Q.lsr_in_gov == 1) { Q.soldiers_lsr -= 2.5; }
  if (Q.sr_in_gov == 1) { Q.soldiers_sr -= 2.5; }            
  if (Q.m_in_gov == 1) { Q.soldiers_m -= 2.5; }
  if (Q.ns_in_gov == 1) { Q.soldiers_ns -= 2.5; }
  if (Q.sdi_in_gov == 1) { Q.soldiers_bsdi -= 2.5; }
  Q.morale *= 0.9; Q.discipline *= 0.8; Q.train_capacity *= 0.95; Q.military_progress -= 2; Q.northern_progress -= 1; Q.western_progress = -3; Q.southwestern_progress = -3; 
!}

>Our casualties: [+ friendly_casualties +]0,000 troops

>Enemy casualties: [+ hostile_casualties +]0,000 troops

@victory
go-to: defeat_desc
on-arrival: {!
  Q.leftcom_strength += 15; Q.leninist_strength -= 5; Q.moderate_strength -= 5
  Q.lsr_strength += 5;
  Q.soldiers_unrest += 5; Q.workers_unrest += 2; Q.peasants_unrest += 2;
  Q.morale *= 1.05; Q.discipline *= 0.95; Q.train_capacity *= 0.95; Q.military_progress -= 1; Q.northern_progress -= 1; Q.western_progress = -2; Q.southwestern_progress = -2; 
!}

>Our casualties: [+ friendly_casualties +]0,000 troops

>Enemy casualties: [+ hostile_casualties +]0,000 troops

And yet at the same time, it appears the German advance does eventually slow, and our own forces manage to regroup and stabilize the front, preventing a complete collapse. 
  
@defeat_desc

[? if northern_progress = -2 : The Germans have captured Riga, and are marching ever closer to Petrograd. ?]
[? if northern_progress = -3 : The Germans have taken Tallinn in Estonia, and are marching ever closer to Petrograd. ?]
[? if northern_progress = -4 : The Germans are at the gates of Petrograd! ?]
[? if western_progress = -3 : In the centre, they've occupied most of Belarussia through Minsk, and are threatening central Russia. ?]
[? if western_progress = -4 : In the centre, they've entered Russia proper and are in a position to threaten many major cities. ?]
[? if southwestern_progress >= -1 : In the centre, they've  pushed the front further back in Galicia and western Ukraine. ?]
[? if southwestern_progress = -2 : In the south, they've entered Ukraine and are threatening Kyiv. ?]
[? if southwestern_progress = -3 : In the south, virtually all of Ukraine has been occupied. ?]

An emergency meeting of the Central Committee is called, where Lenin desperately argues for accepting the peace terms. Still unconvinced, Bukharin argues that the German offensive was anticipated, and that they should keep up the defense. 

[?if peace_position = 2 and (leninist_strength > leftcom_strength) : Trotsky however, fulfilling a verbal agreement he made with Lenin prior, is prepared to abstain so that Lenin's course of action will be approved. 

- @continue
- @peace

@continue
title: We will stay the course and prepare to fight to the last man. 
unavailable-subtitle: The <span style="color: var(--leftcom); font-weight: bold;">Leftcoms</span> do not have the strength to convince the Central Committee. 
choose-if: peace_position = 1 and leftcom_strength > leninist_strength 
on-arrival: {! 
  Q.german_negotiations = 4;
  Q.leftcom_strength += 5; Q.leninist_strength -= 5; Q.moderate_strength -= 5;
  Q.leftcom_dissent -= 5; Q.leninist_dissent += 25; Q.moderate_dissent += 10;
!}

The Central Committee reluctantly decides to continue the fight against Germany, though tensions remain highly charged...

@peace
title: We must make peace with the Germans. 
unavailable-subtitle: The <span style="color: var(--leninist); font-weight: bold;">Leninists</span> do not have the strength to convince the Central Committee. 
on-arrival: {! 
  Q.german_negotiations = 5;
  Q.leftcom_strength -= 5; Q.leninist_strength += 5; Q.moderate_strength += 5;
  Q.leftcom_dissent += 15; Q.leninist_dissent -= 15; Q.moderate_dissent -= 10;
!}

The Central Committee reluctantly accepts the need for peace, though tensions remain highly charged...




